    <!-- Erklär-Datei im Journal-Ordner -->
    <string name="readme_file_name">README.txt</string>
    <string name="readme_text" tools:ignore="TypographyDashes">This is your Relic journal.\n\nEvery day with an entry is its own text file. The files are sorted into folders by year and month, for example:\n\n2026/10/2026-10-09.md\n\nYou can open them with any text editor, even without the Relic app.\n\nHow a file is built:\n\n- At the very top, between two lines of three dashes (---), you find the date and when the entry was created and last changed.\n- Below that is your text. It is written in Markdown: **bold**, *italic*, and lists with a dash at the start of a line.\n- Photos are stored as JPEG files next to the entry (for example 2026-10-09_1.jpg). At the end of the text they are listed again after the line &lt;!-- relic:photos --&gt; so that other programs can show them.\n\nTip: Back up this folder regularly, for example to a computer or the cloud.\n</string>
